::  GENERATED by tools/gen-perf-tests.py -- do not edit.
::
::  The tier-3 WORKLOAD SET (R2.8.1b). One workload per hot path, each
::  asserting the DETERMINISTIC WORK it does; the timing is read off the
::  runner's own `took` line by tools/tier3-noise.py and is deliberately not
::  asserted here -- R2.8.1a measured 0.9%-15.6% run-to-run on unchanged
::  code, so a time is not a fact a test can hold. What IS byte-reproducible
::  is the work, and that is what this file reports.
::
::  NOT A GATE. R2.8.1a's measurement decided tier 3 ships REPORT-ONLY:
::  `release-gate.sh` gets no clause from it. These arms fail only when the
::  port's own work profile CHANGES, which is a regression report, not a
::  threshold.
::
::  Budgets below are measured medians on vere 4.6, --loom 32, carried so a later
::  reader can tell a workload that got slower from one that was always slow.
/+  *test
/=  check  /lib/check
|%
++  prof
  ::  the full statistics of a SAFETY search: generated / distinct / queued /
  ::  depth, and the out-degree distribution the wire run-stats does not carry
  |=  [s=@t c=@t]
  ^-  [@ud @ud @ud @ud [@ud @ud @ud @ud]]
  (run-stats-full:check s c 0 1.000)
::
++  lprof
  ::  the LIVENESS workload's profile, and it is a different arm on purpose:
  ::  `+run-stats-full` builds `bfs-opts` with no liveness at all, so timing a
  ::  temporal spec through it measures the safety search and reports a fast,
  ::  meaningless number. Caught by this file's own capture -- the liveness
  ::  workload's profile came back as its 12-state safety graph. `+run-check`
  ::  is the entry point that actually reaches the 8.2-8.6 engine.
  ::  The leading digit is the verdict (1 = %ok), so a workload that starts
  ::  FAILING rather than merely getting slower shows up in the profile
  |=  [s=@t c=@t]
  ^-  [@ud @ud @ud @ud @ud]
  =/  r  (run-check:check s c 0)
  :-  ?:(?=(%ok -.-.r) 1 0)
  [generated.+.r distinct.+.r queued.+.r depth.+.r]
::
++  test-perf-enum
  ::  hot path: enumeration  (safety engine)
  ::  measured median: 1909 ms median of 15 runs (R2.8.1a: 5 warm + 5 fresh-boot + 5 post-rebuild)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [13 13 0 13 [0 1 1 1]]
  !>  (prof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: ENUMERATION. SUBSET and \\X over small bases, forced inside a\0a\\* quantifier at every state -- the cursor / +force path, not the queue.\0aEXTENDS Integers\0aVARIABLE x\0aInit == x = 0\0aNext == x < 12 /\\ x\' = x + 1\0aInv  == /\\ \\A s \\in SUBSET (1..6) : Card1(s) >= 0\0a        /\\ \\A p \\in (1..8) \\X (1..8) : p[1] >= 1\0aCard1(s) == IF s = {} THEN 0 ELSE 1\0a====\0a' 'INIT Init\0aNEXT Next\0aINVARIANT Inv\0aCHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE\0a')
::
++  test-perf-eval
  ::  hot path: evaluator  (safety engine)
  ::  measured median: 1876 ms median of 15 runs (R2.8.1a: 5 warm + 5 fresh-boot + 5 post-rebuild)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [41 41 0 41 [0 1 1 1]]
  !>  (prof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: the EVALUATOR. The state graph is a line, so almost all the time\0a\\* is +eval over a nested arithmetic/boolean invariant re-solved per state.\0aEXTENDS Integers\0aVARIABLE x\0aInit == x = 0\0aNext == x < 40 /\\ x\' = x + 1\0aHeavy(n) == ((n * n) + (n * 3) - 1) % 7\0aInv == /\\ Heavy(x) >= 0\0a       /\\ Heavy(x + 1) >= 0\0a       /\\ Heavy(x + 2) >= 0\0a       /\\ \\A i \\in 1..12 : Heavy(x + i) >= 0\0a====\0a' 'INIT Init\0aNEXT Next\0aINVARIANT Inv\0aCHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE\0a')
::
++  test-perf-ex-coffeecan
  ::  hot path: liveness  (liveness engine)
  ::  measured median: 3718 ms median of 5 warm runs (R4.P9, 2026-10-12)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [1 452 135 0 1]
  !>  (lprof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: LIVENESS AT SCALE (R4.P9). tlaplus-Examples CoffeeCan (MIT,\0a\\* Examples@47b0e2cc0 specifications/CoffeeCan/CoffeeCan.tla) with all four of its\0a\\* properties; the module body below is the upstream one, unchanged.\0aEXTENDS Naturals\0a\0aCONSTANT MaxBeanCount\0a\0aASSUME MaxBeanFact == MaxBeanCount \\in Nat /\\ MaxBeanCount >= 1\0a\0aVARIABLES can\0a\0a\\* The set of all possible cans\0aCan == [black : 0..MaxBeanCount, white : 0..MaxBeanCount]\0a\0a\\* Possible values the can variable can take on\0aTypeInvariant == can \\in Can\0a\0a\\* Initialize can so it contains between 1 and MaxBeanCount beans\0aInit == can \\in {c \\in Can : c.black + c.white \\in 1..MaxBeanCount}\0a\0a\\* Number of beans currently in the can\0aBeanCount == can.black + can.white\0a\0a\\* Pick two black beans; throw both away, put one black bean in\0aPickSameColorBlack ==\0a    /\\ BeanCount > 1\0a    /\\ can.black >= 2\0a    /\\ can\' = [can EXCEPT !.black = @ - 1]\0a\0a\\* Pick two white beans; throw both away, put one black bean in\0aPickSameColorWhite ==\0a    /\\ BeanCount > 1\0a    /\\ can.white >= 2\0a    /\\ can\' = [can EXCEPT !.black = @ + 1, !.white = @ - 2]\0a\0a\\* Pick one bean of each color; put white back, throw away black\0aPickDifferentColor ==\0a    /\\ BeanCount > 1\0a    /\\ can.black >= 1\0a    /\\ can.white >= 1\0a    /\\ can\' = [can EXCEPT !.black = @ - 1]\0a\0a\\* Termination action to avoid triggering deadlock detection\0aTermination ==\0a    /\\ BeanCount = 1\0a    /\\ UNCHANGED can\0a\0a\\* Next-state relation: what actions can be taken?\0aNext ==\0a    \\/ PickSameColorWhite\0a    \\/ PickSameColorBlack\0a    \\/ PickDifferentColor\0a    \\/ Termination\0a\0a\\* Action formula: every step decreases the number of beans in the can\0aMonotonicDecrease == [][BeanCount\' < BeanCount]_can\0a\0a\\* Liveness property: we eventually end up with one bean left\0aEventuallyTerminates == <>(ENABLED Termination)\0a\0a\\* Loop invariant: every step preserves white bean count mod 2\0aLoopInvariant == [][can.white % 2 = 0 <=> can\'.white % 2 = 0]_can\0a\0a\\* Hypothesis: If we start out with an even number of white beans, we end up\0a\\* with a single black bean. Otherwise, we end up with a single white bean.\0aTerminationHypothesis ==\0a    IF can.white % 2 = 0\0a    THEN <>(can.black = 1 /\\ can.white = 0)\0a    ELSE <>(can.black = 0 /\\ can.white = 1)\0a\0a\\* Start out in a state defined by the Init operator and every step is one\0a\\* defined by the Next operator. Assume weak fairness so the system can\'t\0a\\* stutter indefinitely: we eventually take some beans out of the can.\0aSpec ==\0a    /\\ Init\0a    /\\ [][Next]_can\0a    /\\ WF_can(Next)\0a\0a\\* What we want to show: that if our system follows the rules set out by the\0a\\* Spec operator, then all our properties and assumptions will be satisfied.\0aTHEOREM Spec =>\0a    /\\ TypeInvariant\0a    /\\ MonotonicDecrease\0a    /\\ EventuallyTerminates\0a    /\\ LoopInvariant\0a    /\\ TerminationHypothesis\0a\0a====\0a' 'CONSTANTS MaxBeanCount = 15\0aSPECIFICATION Spec\0aPROPERTY EventuallyTerminates MonotonicDecrease LoopInvariant TerminationHypothesis\0aINVARIANTS TypeInvariant\0a')
::
++  test-perf-ex-gameoflife
  ::  hot path: sets  (safety engine)
  ::  measured median: 2750 ms median of 5 warm runs (R4.P9, 2026-10-12)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [32 16 0 1 [0 0 0 0]]
  !>  (prof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: SET- AND FUNCTION-HEAVY STATES (R4.P9). tlaplus-Examples GameOfLife\0a\\* (MIT, Examples@47b0e2cc0 specifications/GameOfLife/GameOfLife.tla), body unchanged.\0aEXTENDS Integers\0a\0aCONSTANT N\0aVARIABLE grid\0a\0aASSUME N \\in Nat\0a\0avars == grid\0a\0aRECURSIVE Sum(_, _)\0aSum(f, S) == IF S = {} THEN 0\0a                       ELSE LET x == CHOOSE x \\in S : TRUE\0a                            IN  f[x] + Sum(f, S \\ {x})\0a                            \0aPos == {<<x, y>> : x, y \\in 1..N}\0aTypeOK == grid \\in [Pos -> BOOLEAN]\0a\0asc[<<x, y>> \\in (0 .. N + 1) \\X\0a                (0 .. N + 1)] == CASE \\/ x = 0 \\/ y = 0\0a                                      \\/ x > N \\/ y > N\0a                                      \\/ ~grid[<<x, y>>] -> 0\0a                                   [] OTHER -> 1\0a\0ascore(p) == LET nbrs == {x \\in {-1, 0, 1} \\X\0a                               {-1, 0, 1} : x /= <<0, 0>>}\0a                points == {<<p[1] + x, p[2] + y>> : <<x, y>> \\in nbrs}\0a            IN Sum(sc, points)\0a                   \0aInit == grid \\in [Pos -> BOOLEAN]\0aNext == grid\' = [p \\in Pos |-> IF \\/  (grid[p] /\\ score(p) \\in {2, 3})\0a                                  \\/ (~grid[p] /\\ score(p) = 3)\0a                                THEN TRUE\0a                                ELSE FALSE]\0a\0aSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\0a\0a====\0a' 'CONSTANT N = 2\0aINVARIANT TypeOK\0aSPECIFICATION Spec\0a')
::
++  test-perf-fp
  ::  hot path: fingerprinting  (safety engine)
  ::  measured median: 2677 ms median of 15 runs (R2.8.1a: 5 warm + 5 fresh-boot + 5 post-rebuild)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [61 61 0 61 [0 1 1 1]]
  !>  (prof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: FINGERPRINTING. Every state carries a record and a sequence, so\0a\\* each dedup pays a full structural +fp-enc rather than an integer one.\0aEXTENDS Integers, Sequences\0aVARIABLE r\0aInit == r = [a |-> 0, b |-> <<0, 0, 0>>, c |-> "z"]\0aNext == /\\ r.a < 60\0a        /\\ r\' = [a |-> r.a + 1,\0a                 b |-> <<r.a, r.a + 1, r.a + 2>>,\0a                 c |-> r.c]\0aInv  == r.a >= 0\0a====\0a' 'INIT Init\0aNEXT Next\0aINVARIANT Inv\0aCHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE\0a')
